From 859ed22a7ba883f9517119fcccfb67b2f3dcac6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:36:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fs): accept native document paths spelled through a
 canonical ancestor

Owner request: TODO delivery 0 (deterministic verify:delivery) and OV-114
(native canvas documents must save inside any real workspace).

Reason: resolveNativeFileBoundary compared the requested path only with
boundaryRoot and its realpath. A path reaching the same workspace through
another spelling (macOS /var -> /private/var, or a workspace alias) was
denied with permission_denied. The 2026-10-14 acceptance passed only
because TMPDIR then had no symlinked ancestor; with the default macOS
TMPDIR six native-file cases failed.

Change: also accept a path whose nearest ancestor canonicalizes to the
workspace root; segments below that ancestor stay literal, so symlinks
inside the workspace are still rejected. Tests now create canonical temp
roots, and the plugin cwd assertion compares canonical paths.
Upstream: native document boundaries are Fleet-authored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
